Customer Purchase Prediction Using K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

1. Project Overview

This project focuses on predicting customer purchase behavior using Machine Learning. The K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) classification algorithm is used to predict whether a customer will make a purchase based on customer-related attributes.

The project explores feature selection, data preprocessing, feature scaling, hyperparameter tuning, and model evaluation to understand how different customer attributes influence prediction performance.

2. Project Objectives

- Develop a machine learning model to predict customer purchase behavior.
- Analyze customer data using exploratory data analysis.
- Understand the importance of feature selection.
- Apply feature scaling using StandardScaler.
- Optimize the KNN model by experimenting with different K values.
- Evaluate model performance using classification metrics.

 3. Technologies and Libraries

- Programming Language: Python
- Data Analysis: Pandas, NumPy
- Data Visualization: Matplotlib, Seaborn
- Machine Learning: Scikit-learn
- Development Environment: Google Colab

 4. Dataset Description

The dataset contains 1,500 customer records and 9 columns, including 8 input features and 1 target variable.

 Input Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| Age | Customer age |
| Gender | Customer gender |
| AnnualIncome | Customer annual income |
| NumberOfPurchases | Number of purchases made |
| ProductCategory | Product category |
| TimeSpentOnWebsite | Time spent on the website |
| LoyaltyProgram | Customer loyalty program participation |
| DiscountsAvailed | Number of discounts availed |

 Target Variable

PurchaseStatus

- 0: No Purchase
- 1: Purchase

 5. Project Workflow

1. Import the required Python libraries.
2. Load the customer dataset using Pandas.
3. Perform data exploration and inspection.
4. Conduct exploratory data analysis using Seaborn and Matplotlib.
5. Separate input features and the target variable.
6. Split the dataset into training and testing sets using an 80:20 ratio.
7. Apply feature scaling using StandardScaler.
8. Build and train the KNN classification model.
9. Generate predictions using the test dataset.
10. Evaluate model performance.
11. Perform hyperparameter tuning using cross-validation.

 6. Algorithm: K-Nearest Neighbors

K-Nearest Neighbors is a supervised Machine Learning algorithm used for classification and regression tasks.

In this project, KNN predicts customer purchase status by identifying the nearest data points based on feature distances. The final prediction is determined through majority voting among the selected nearest neighbors.

StandardScaler is used to normalize feature scales before applying the KNN algorithm.

